What was it in English? I thought it would be something like "I'll do all I
can for you" rather than "I'll make sure everything that can be done for
you gets done".

In any case, I'm just not too happy with "jai". The way I understand it, it
is used for sumti raising, i.e. extract an argument from a subordinate
bridi in the x1 of a selbri and raise it to become the first argument of
the selbri. Here you seem to use it to create an event out of a property?

mu'o mi'e xorxes
.

